    "diagnosis": "Cystic Mesenchymal Hamartoma",
    "title": "",
    "legend": "Mesenchymal hamartoma diagnosed in a 2 year-old with an 8.5 cm, multicystic liver mass. Cysts are lined by cuboidal and columnar epithelium and surrounded by loose to dense stroma, containing focally branching bile ducts, clusters of hepatocytes with eosinophilic cytoplasm, and blood vessels.",
    "source": "Dolores H. López-Terrada",
    "copyright": "",
    "tablehtml": "",
